{
  "version": 1,
  "title": "JsonUI responsive \u2014 which key of a responsive block wins, shared test vectors",
  "notes": "The rule shared/core/responsive_resolver.rb gives every codegen (build_branches: the first branch whose condition holds), and both Dynamic runtimes follow. One key wins alone; its overrides go on the base, and no other key's do. Size classes: the first key of PRIORITY_ORDER (regular-landscape, medium-landscape, compact-landscape, landscape, regular, medium, compact) that is in the block and holds. env.sizeClass is the width bucket (Android: compact < 600dp <= medium < 840dp <= regular); on iOS compact and medium are both horizontalSizeClass .compact, so medium and medium-landscape hold wherever compact and compact-landscape do \u2014 ios_winner, where present, is the iOS answer. Width conditions (jui-responsive-width-threshold-conditions): minWidth:N holds when env.width >= N, maxWidth:N when env.width < N; the smallest maxWidth that holds wins, else the largest minWidth that holds. env.width is the window's width in pt / dp / CSS px. winner null: no key holds, the base is drawn. Read by: sjui/kjui/rjui responsive_resolver specs, jui_tools tests, SwiftJsonUI ResponsiveResolverVectorTests, KotlinJsonUI ResponsiveResolverVectorTest (copies checked byte for byte by each library's CI). key_cases: whether a key is a width condition, and which (null: it is not one \u2014 a size class, or a misspelling jui build refuses when it looks like one).",
